{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Keyboard Shortcuts","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"role":"collectionGroup"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem"],"anchor":"Guides"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/keyboardshortcuts"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How keyboard input flows through TUIkit: from raw terminal bytes to your view handlers."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Input Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/QuitBehavior"],"anchor":"Input-Types"},{"title":"Focus","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusState","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable"],"anchor":"Focus"},{"title":"Status Bar","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBar","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarItem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarItemProtocol","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Shortcut"],"anchor":"Status-Bar"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit uses a layered event dispatch system. When a key is pressed, it passes through up to five layers. The first layer that consumes the event wins: remaining layers are skipped. Layer 0 (text input) and Layer 3 (focus system) are mutually exclusive: when a text input element is focused, Layer 0 runs and Layer 3 is skipped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"keyboard-event-dispatch.png","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Additionally, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Ctrl+C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (SIGINT) is handled at the OS signal level ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" any of these layers: it always terminates the application.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Available Keys","type":"heading","anchor":"Available-Keys"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Key","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enum defines all keys that TUIkit can recognize from terminal input:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Character Keys","type":"heading","anchor":"Character-Keys"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any printable character is represented as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".character(Character)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".onKeyPress(Key.from(\"x\")) {","    \/\/ handle \"x\" key","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Uppercase detection: when a capital letter is typed, the resulting "},{"code":"KeyEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has "},{"code":"shift: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" set automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Special Keys","type":"heading","anchor":"Special-Keys"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Description","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".escape"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Escape key"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".enter","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enter \/ Return"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".tab"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tab"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".backspace","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Backspace \/ Delete backward"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".delete","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Forward delete","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"text":"Arrow Keys","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Arrow-Keys"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Description","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".up","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Arrow up"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".down"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Arrow down"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".left"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Arrow left","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".right","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Arrow right","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"text":"Navigation Keys","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Navigation-Keys"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Description","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".home"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Home","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".end","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"End"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".pageUp"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Page Up"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".pageDown"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Page Down"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"text":"Key Events and Modifiers","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Key-Events-and-Modifiers"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyEvent"},{"type":"text","text":" combines a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Key"},{"type":"text","text":" with modifier flags:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct KeyEvent {","    public let key: Key","    public let ctrl: Bool     \/\/ Ctrl modifier","    public let alt: Bool      \/\/ Alt \/ Option modifier","    public let shift: Bool    \/\/ Shift modifier","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The terminal encodes modifiers differently from GUI frameworks:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ctrl+letter"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Detected from ASCII control codes (0x01–0x1A). For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Ctrl+C"},{"type":"text","text":" produces byte "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0x03"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Alt+key"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Detected from ESC prefix sequences (","type":"text"},{"code":"ESC","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" followed by the key byte).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shift"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Only auto-detected for uppercase letters. The terminal does not send distinct shift codes for most keys."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"text":"Registering Key Handlers","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Registering-Key-Handlers"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onKeyPress()"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier to handle keyboard events in your views:"}]},{"text":"Handle All Keys","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Handle-All-Keys"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["Text(\"Press any key\")","    .onKeyPress { event in","        if event.key == .enter {","            doSomething()","            return true   \/\/ consumed: stops propagation","        }","        return false      \/\/ not consumed: passes to next handler","    }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Handle Specific Keys","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Handle-Specific-Keys"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["Text(\"Use arrow keys\")","    .onKeyPress(keys: [.up, .down]) { event in","        if event.key == .up { moveUp() }","        else { moveDown() }","        return true","    }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Handle a Single Key","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Handle-a-Single-Key"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The single-key variant always consumes the event:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["Text(\"Press Enter to continue\")","    .onKeyPress(.enter) {","        continueAction()","    }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Handler Priority","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Handler-Priority"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Handlers are dispatched in "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"reverse registration order","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the deepest view in the tree (most recently registered) gets the event first. This means inner views can intercept events before outer views see them."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["VStack {","    Text(\"Outer\")","        .onKeyPress(.enter) {","            \/\/ Only reached if inner handler did NOT consume it","            print(\"outer enter\")","        }","    Text(\"Inner\")","        .onKeyPress(.enter) {","            \/\/ Gets the event FIRST","            print(\"inner enter\")","        }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All key handlers are re-registered every render frame. If a view is not rendered (e.g. behind a conditional), its handlers are not active."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"text":"Focus Navigation","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Focus-Navigation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"},{"type":"text","text":" dispatches key events in three steps:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Focused element delegation"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": the focused element’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called first. If it consumes the event, dispatch stops.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tab \/ Shift+Tab","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": cycles focus between elements (wraps around).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Arrow key fallback","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Up\/Left move to the previous element in the section, Down\/Right move to the next. This only triggers if the focused element did not consume the arrow key in step 1.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tab","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Move focus to the next focusable element (wraps around)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shift+Tab"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Move focus to the previous focusable element (wraps around)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Up \/ Left","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Move to previous element in section (fallback)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Down \/ Right","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Move to next element in section (fallback)","type":"text"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more details, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Default Bindings","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Default-Bindings"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer 4 provides three built-in key bindings that work without any configuration:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Condition"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Q"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Quit application","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only when "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/QuitBehavior"},{"type":"text","text":" allows it"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"t"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"}],"type":"paragraph